---
import '../../styles/reset.css';
import '../../styles/globals.css';
import TitleCard from '../../components/cyber/TitleCard.astro';
import OldBugs from '../../components/cyber/OldBugs.astro';
import Headlines from '../../components/cyber/Headlines.astro';
import PhpGrid from '../../components/cyber/PhpGrid.astro';
import Freezer from '../../components/cyber/Freezer.astro';
import PasswordAttacks from '../../components/cyber/PasswordAttacks.astro';
import OnlineOffline from '../../components/cyber/OnlineOffline.astro';
import Breach from '../../components/cyber/Breach.astro';
import Updates from '../../components/cyber/Updates.astro';
import PasswordManager from '../../components/cyber/PasswordManager.astro';
import PasswordStrength from '../../components/cyber/PasswordStrength.astro';
import TwoFactor from '../../components/cyber/TwoFactor.astro';
import Router from '../../components/cyber/Router.astro';
import FakeCaptcha from '../../components/cyber/FakeCaptcha.astro';
import FakeVirus from '../../components/cyber/FakeVirus.astro';
import VoiceClone from '../../components/cyber/VoiceClone.astro';
import Checklist from '../../components/cyber/Checklist.astro';

// Speaker notes, one per slide, in order.
const notes = [
  'Quick one: security has changed a lot, even in the last month. Two parts: what is going on, then what to actually do.',
  'Part 1. The short version: things are kind of crazy right now.',
  'AI got really good at reading code. It is finding bugs that sat unnoticed for 15, 20, almost 30 years, in software everything runs on.',
  'Bugs that let someone take over a device just because it is on the internet used to show up maybe once a year. Now it is several a week. Record 72,000 vulnerabilities this year, double last year, and attackers use new bugs within a day. Attackers can now hand AI a whole attack and it does the steps for them.',
  'PHP runs about 70% of websites. A bug from 2012 let anyone run code on those servers. Attacks started before the fix. NSA and FBI said patch it or take the site offline. That was a long day at work.',
  'It is not just computers. Hackers set supermarket freezers to defrost. Anything on the internet can be attacked.',
  'At the peak Microsoft blocked about 7,000 password attacks a second, around 600 million a day. This year it finally dropped 26%, because 2FA and passkeys work. So attackers switched to fake login pages that steal your session, and paste-this-command scams.',
  'What counts as a password attack: bots guessing at real login pages. That is what Microsoft can count. The scarier kind happens offline after a breach, and nobody can count it.',
  'Breaches are constant. Some random site leaks your email and password, and bots try that combo on your email, bank, Amazon. Reused password, they are in. This is why you never reuse or share passwords.',
  'Part 2. Good news: the fixes are simple. Antivirus is not the big thing anymore. Updates and passwords are.',
  'Number one: updates. I know they are annoying, and half the time nothing looks different afterward. That is because what changed is usually a security fix you cannot see. And yes, sometimes they move things around. Relearning a button beats getting hacked. Turn on automatic updates everywhere and restart when it asks.',
  'You cannot remember a unique password for every site, so do not try. A password manager remembers them all and makes up random ones. You remember one long passphrase. The vault syncs through their cloud, but it is locked with that passphrase, so the company cannot read it. Bonus: it will not autofill on a fake lookalike site, which catches phishing. Bitwarden is free, or just use the one built into your iPhone or Chrome.',
  'Strong does not mean symbols. It means long and random. Symbol rules are lazy code. Use a password manager and let it generate them.',
  'Turn on 2FA for the accounts people actually try to break into: email first (it resets everything else), bank, password manager. App codes or passkeys beat text messages. And never approve a sign-in pop-up you did not start, even if it keeps coming. It means someone has your password.',
  'Your router sees everything your house sends. Most of it is encrypted now, but a hacked router can still see where you go, send you to fake sites, attack your other gadgets, and rent your connection to criminals. Old routers stop getting fixes and get hacked in bulk. If yours is 5+ years old, replace it.',
  'Real, normal websites get hacked and show fake checks like this. A real check never asks you to press keys or paste anything. Microsoft saw this on 1.1 million devices in three months.',
  'Websites cannot scan your computer. Close the tab, never call the number.',
  'AI can clone a voice from a short clip. Urgent, secret, and money together means scam. Hang up and reach them another way, or ask something only the real person would know.',
  'That is the list. On extensions: fake AI assistant extensions got about 900,000 installs this year, so only keep ones you trust. Pick one or two today: updates and a password manager get you most of the way.',
  'Questions? Happy to help anyone set up a password manager or check their router after this.',
];
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-deck>
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  <title>Trevor Loula | Staying Safe Online in 2026 (slides)</title>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="deck">
    <div class="slides">
      <section class="slide"><TitleCard kicker="cyber-hygiene --year 2026" title="Staying safe online in 2026" sub="What changed, and the handful of things that actually matter now." /></section>
      <section class="slide"><TitleCard kicker="part 1" title="What's going on" sub="AI, ancient bugs, and a lot of password guessing." /></section>
      <section class="slide"><OldBugs /></section>
      <section class="slide"><Headlines /></section>
      <section class="slide"><PhpGrid /></section>
      <section class="slide"><Freezer /></section>
      <section class="slide"><PasswordAttacks /></section>
      <section class="slide"><OnlineOffline /></section>
      <section class="slide"><Breach /></section>
      <section class="slide"><TitleCard kicker="part 2" title="What to do about it" sub="No antivirus shopping required." /></section>
      <section class="slide"><Updates /></section>
      <section class="slide"><PasswordManager /></section>
      <section class="slide"><PasswordStrength /></section>
      <section class="slide"><TwoFactor /></section>
      <section class="slide"><Router /></section>
      <section class="slide"><FakeCaptcha /></section>
      <section class="slide"><FakeVirus /></section>
      <section class="slide"><VoiceClone /></section>
      <section class="slide"><Checklist /></section>
      <section class="slide"><TitleCard kicker="exit 0" title="That's it. Questions?" sub="Now go turn on automatic updates. I'll wait." /></section>
    </div>
    <aside class="notes" hidden>
      <div class="notes-count cs-mono"></div>
      <p class="notes-text"></p>
    </aside>
    <div class="progress"><i></i></div>
    <div class="hint">← → to navigate · R replay · N notes · F fullscreen</div>
  </main>
  <script type="application/json" id="deck-notes" set:html={JSON.stringify(notes)} />
</body>
</html>

<script>
  import { playScene, resetScene } from '../../scripts/cyber-scene';

  const slides = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide'));
  const notes: string[] = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('deck-notes')!.textContent || '[]');
  const notesEl = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.notes')!;
  const bar = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.progress i')!;
  let idx = Math.min(slides.length - 1, Math.max(0, (parseInt(location.hash.slice(1)) || 1) - 1));

  function sceneOf(i: number) {
    return slides[i].querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene]')!;
  }

  function show(i: number, force = false) {
    const next = Math.min(slides.length - 1, Math.max(0, i));
    // At the first/last slide, don't replay the same slide on "next"/"back"
    if (next === idx && !force) return;
    idx = next;
    slides.forEach((s, n) => {
      s.classList.toggle('active', n === idx);
      if (n !== idx) resetScene(sceneOf(n));
    });
    playScene(sceneOf(idx));
    bar.style.width = `${((idx + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
    notesEl.querySelector('.notes-count')!.textContent = `${idx + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
    notesEl.querySelector('.notes-text')!.textContent = notes[idx] ?? '';
    try {
      history.replaceState(null, '', `#${idx + 1}`);
    } catch {
      // Sandboxed previews (e.g. srcdoc iframes) don't allow URL changes
    }
  }

  document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.altKey) return;
    switch (e.key) {
      case 'ArrowRight': case 'ArrowDown': case 'PageDown': case ' ': case 'Enter':
        e.preventDefault(); show(idx + 1); break;
      case 'ArrowLeft': case 'ArrowUp': case 'PageUp': case 'Backspace':
        e.preventDefault(); show(idx - 1); break;
      case 'Home': show(0); break;
      case 'End': show(slides.length - 1); break;
      case 'r': case 'R': playScene(sceneOf(idx)); break;
      case 'n': case 'N': notesEl.hidden = !notesEl.hidden; break;
      case 'f': case 'F':
        if (document.fullscreenElement) document.exitFullscreen();
        else document.documentElement.requestFullscreen?.();
        break;
    }
  });

  document.querySelector('.slides')!.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const x = (e as MouseEvent).clientX;
    show(x < window.innerWidth / 3 ? idx - 1 : idx + 1);
  });

  // Swipe on phones/tablets
  let touchX = 0;
  document.addEventListener('touchstart', (e) => { touchX = e.touches[0].clientX; }, { passive: true });
  document.addEventListener('touchend', (e) => {
    const dx = e.changedTouches[0].clientX - touchX;
    if (Math.abs(dx) > 50) show(dx < 0 ? idx + 1 : idx - 1);
  });

  show(idx, true);
</script>

<style is:global>
  html, body { height: 100%; background: #000; color: #e8e8e8; font-family: 'Geist', sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }
  .deck { height: 100vh; height: 100dvh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0; max-width: none; gap: 0; }
  .slides { position: relative; width: min(100vw, calc(100dvh * 16 / 9)); aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; cursor: pointer; }
  .slide { position: absolute; inset: 0; opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; transition: opacity .35s ease; }
  .slide.active { opacity: 1; pointer-events: auto; }
  .slide .cyber-scene { margin: 0; height: 100%; }
  .slide .cs-stage { height: 100%; border: none; background: #000; }
  .slide .cs-caption { display: none; }
  .notes { position: fixed; left: 1rem; right: 1rem; bottom: 1.5rem; max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; background: rgba(15,15,15,.95); border: 1px solid #2a2a2a; padding: .9rem 1.2rem; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.5; z-index: 5; }
  .notes p { margin: .3rem 0 0; }
  .notes-count { color: #a277ff; font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; font-size: .8rem; }
  .progress { position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; height: 3px; background: #111; }
  .progress i { display: block; height: 100%; width: 0; background: #8c5cf5; transition: width .3s ease; }
  .hint { position: fixed; top: .6rem; right: .9rem; font-size: .75rem; color: #555; font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace; }
  @media (hover: none) { .hint { display: none; } }
</style>
